  "text": "Recipe: Quinoa Handvo - Uthapam Style\nCreator: Mrs N K Manku\nCategory: Pancake\nIngredients: quinoa, seven different daals, methi dana (fenugreek seeds), water, bottle gourd, pumpkin, red onion, carrot, capsicum, beetroot, hing (asafoetida), black pepper, ginger, dates, maple syrup, green chillies, pink salt, lemon juice, curry leaves, ENO, mustard seeds, cumin seeds, sesame seeds, crushed peanuts\nCooking methods: blend, roast, saute, air-fry, microwave\nInstructions: BATTER:\n- 1 cup quinoa, 1 cup of seven different daals (beans of our choice), 1/2 tsp methi dana (fenugreek seeds) – soak overnight, rinse well, add 3 tsp water, grind it & keep for 6 to 8 hours for fermentation.\n- Prepare 1.5 cups of grated mixed veggies of your choice. I used bottle gourd, pumpkin, red onion, carrot, capsicum, beetroot. Squeeze the juice out of grated veggies with hands to make them less watery – use this juice as a vegetable broth for another recipe.\n- Mix grated mixed vegetables with fermented batter. Add 1/4 tsp hing (asafoetida), 1/2 tsp black pepper, 1 inch ginger (grated), 1 tsp sweetener (dates | maple syrup), some green chillies (to taste), 1/4 tsp pink salt (to taste), a few drops of lemon juice, 3-4 curry leaves (minced). Finally add 1 tsp ENO just before cooking the batter.\n\nROASTED MASALA:\n- Dry roast mustard seeds, cumin seeds, curry leaves, sesame seeds and some crushed peanuts.\n\nDivide the batter into three equal portions.\n+ UTHAPAM STYLE HANDVO: Pour one portion of batter on non-stick pan. Prepare like uthapam. Garnish with roasted masala. Cook for 5 to 8 minutes on slow flame, covered with a lid. Then flip it over and cook for another 5 to 8 minutes.\n+ AIR FRIED HANDVO: Air fry the second portion of batter for 15 mins each side at 180 C.\n+ MICROWAVED HANDVO: Pour the third portion of batter into mugs. Microwave for 3 mins.\nNotes: Use juice from grated veggies as a vegetable broth for another recipe.",
